Subject: [PATCH] wgl: present windows opaque through kopper

stw_st_fill_private_loader_data() set has_alpha for every window, so Zink's
Win32 swapchain asked for VK_COMPOSITE_ALPHA_PRE_MULTIPLIED, and the Win32
WSI created its DXGI composition swapchain with
DXGI_ALPHA_MODE_PREMULTIPLIED. DWM then blended whatever alpha an
application left in its back buffer with the desktop behind the window.
Blender 4.2 leaves alpha below one in much of its UI, and its window was
translucent on Windows 10. The OpenGL probe writes alpha one and was opaque.

A WGL window is opaque on Windows: GDI and DWM's redirection surfaces
ignore the framebuffer's alpha. The swapchain now asks for
VK_COMPOSITE_ALPHA_OPAQUE, which the WSI maps to DXGI_ALPHA_MODE_IGNORE.

Evidence: docs/present.md, docs/evidence/present/ (src/gl_alpha.c).
Origin: vmlab-win3d present worker.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/wgl/stw_st.c b/src/gallium/frontends/wgl/stw_st.c
index 06506ef..0506be5 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/wgl/stw_st.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/wgl/stw_st.c
@@ -141,7 +141,12 @@ stw_st_fill_private_loader_data(struct stw_st_framebuffer *stwfb, struct kopper_
    win32->flags = 0;
    win32->hinstance = GetModuleHandle(NULL);
    win32->hwnd = stwfb->fb->hWnd;
-   out->has_alpha = true;
+   /* A WGL window is opaque on Windows: GDI and DWM's redirection surfaces
+    * ignore the framebuffer's alpha. Kopper's Win32 swapchain is a DXGI
+    * composition swapchain whose alpha mode follows this flag, so with
+    * alpha the compositor would blend whatever alpha the application left
+    * in its back buffer with the desktop behind the window. */
+   out->has_alpha = false;
 }
 #endif
